IMPORT `law08-ch3-products`

-- Tests for Dieu 87-93. V1 pinned at 1 June 2025, V2 at 1 March 2026, V3 at 1 August 2026.

§ `Tests: Dieu 87-93`

§§ `Dieu 87(2)`

@@q 1760 1775
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1760-1775)
@@fx `rules, terms and rates that comply in full` : `Rules, terms and rates` ; `comply with the law and fit Vietnamese practice, ethics, culture and custom` = TRUE ; `the language of the rules and terms is accurate, simple and easy to understand and technical terms are defined` = TRUE ; `state clearly insurable interest, object, scope and risks, the rights and duties of the policyholder and insured person, the insurer's liability, exclusions, the method of paying and the dispute provisions` = TRUE ; `premium is built on statistics, corresponds to the conditions and liability and ensures solvency` = TRUE
@@fx `rules, terms and rates with jargon` : `Rules, terms and rates` ; `comply with the law and fit Vietnamese practice, ethics, culture and custom` = TRUE ; `state clearly insurable interest, object, scope and risks, the rights and duties of the policyholder and insured person, the insurer's liability, exclusions, the method of paying and the dispute provisions` = TRUE ; `premium is built on statistics, corresponds to the conditions and liability and ensures solvency` = TRUE
@@fx `rules, terms and rates with a premium not built on statistics` : `Rules, terms and rates` ; `comply with the law and fit Vietnamese practice, ethics, culture and custom` = TRUE ; `the language of the rules and terms is accurate, simple and easy to understand and technical terms are defined` = TRUE ; `state clearly insurable interest, object, scope and risks, the rights and duties of the policyholder and insured person, the insurer's liability, exclusions, the method of paying and the dispute provisions` = TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 87(2): the rules, terms and rates meet the requirements` `rules, terms and rates that comply in full`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 87(2): the rules, terms and rates meet the requirements` `rules, terms and rates with jargon`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 87(2): the rules, terms and rates meet the requirements` `rules, terms and rates with a premium not built on statistics`

§§ `Dieu 87(3) and (3a): the premium method, by vintage`

@@q 1776 1782
@@qa 165 178
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1776-1782; src:law139-2025-qh15:165-178)
@@fx `a life method registered and approved` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a life insurance product` ; `registered with the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE ; `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE
@@fx `a life method registered but not approved` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a life insurance product` ; `registered with the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE
@@fx `a health method registered and approved` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a health insurance product` ; `registered with the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE ; `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE
@@fx `a motor method registered and approved, not notified` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product` ; `registered with the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE ; `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE
@@fx `a motor method notified and applied, never registered` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product` ; `notified in writing to the Ministry of Finance before it was applied or changed` = TRUE ; `the insurer applies the method it notified` = TRUE
@@fx `a motor method notified but not followed` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product` ; `notified in writing to the Ministry of Finance before it was applied or changed` = TRUE
@@fx `a compulsory motor liability method` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners` ; `registered with the Ministry of Finance` = TRUE
@@fx `a method for another non-life product, nothing done` : `A premium method` ; `product line` = `another non-life insurance product`
-- life and health: the same in all three vintages
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered and approved`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered and approved`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered and approved`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered but not approved`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered but not approved`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a health method registered and approved`)
-- voluntary motor: approval in V1, notice from V2
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method registered and approved, not notified`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method registered and approved, not notified`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method registered and approved, not notified`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method notified and applied, never registered`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method notified and applied, never registered`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method notified and applied, never registered`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a motor method notified but not followed`)
-- compulsory motor liability: neither article governs its premium
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a compulsory motor liability method`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a compulsory motor liability method`)
-- another non-life product: no requirement
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a method for another non-life product, nothing done`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a method for another non-life product, nothing done`)
-- before the Law took effect
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2022 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` `a life method registered and approved`)

#ASSERT count `Dieu 87(4): the ways an insurer may offer products` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 87(5): the Government's rules on the dossier, order and procedure to register or notify a premium method`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 87(6): the Minister of Finance's rules on premium methods and on supplying products`

§§ `Dieu 88 and 89`

@@q 1796 1855
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 88(2): the Government's rules on the measures supporting agricultural, forestry, fishery and social-security products`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 89(1): the foreign reinsurer meets the credit rating and the other conditions the Government sets`
@@fx `a licensed insurer co-insuring` : `A would-be co-insurer` ; `is an insurer or a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` = TRUE ; `holds a licence to establish and operate under this Law` = TRUE
@@fx `an unlicensed insurer co-insuring` : `A would-be co-insurer` ; `is an insurer or a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` = TRUE
@@fx `a reinsurer co-insuring` : `A would-be co-insurer` ; `holds a licence to establish and operate under this Law` = TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 89(2): the enterprise may take part in co-insurance` `a licensed insurer co-insuring`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 89(2): the enterprise may take part in co-insurance` `an unlicensed insurer co-insuring`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 89(2): the enterprise may take part in co-insurance` `a reinsurer co-insuring`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 89(5): the Minister of Finance's rules on reinsurance, ceding and co-insurance`

§§ `Dieu 90`

@@q 1857 1925
@ref Dieu 90 (src:1857-1925)
@@fx `outsourcing of claims handling` : `An outsourcing`
@@fx `outsourcing of internal audit` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourced activity is internal audit` = TRUE
@@fx `outsourcing of internal control` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourced activity is internal control` = TRUE
@@fx `outsourcing of risk management` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourced activity is risk management` = TRUE
@@fx `outsourcing of selling` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourced activity is advising on, introducing or offering insurance products or arranging the making of insurance contracts` = TRUE
@@fx `a provider that performs 75 percent itself` : `An outsourcing` ; `share of the value of the work the provider performs itself` = 75%
@@fx `a provider that performs 74 percent itself` : `An outsourcing` ; `share of the value of the work the provider performs itself` = 74%
@@fx `a provider that performs 80 percent and subcontracts without consent` : `An outsourcing` ; `share of the value of the work the provider performs itself` = 80% ; `part of the work is subcontracted` = TRUE
@@fx `a provider that performs 80 percent and subcontracts with consent` : `An outsourcing` ; `share of the value of the work the provider performs itself` = 80% ; `part of the work is subcontracted` = TRUE ; `the insurer consented to the subcontract in writing in advance` = TRUE
@@fx `a complete outsourcing contract` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourcing contract is in writing` = TRUE ; `the contract states scope and content` = TRUE ; `the contract states time and place` = TRUE ; `the contract states the rights and obligations of both sides` = TRUE ; `the contract states quality standards and requirements` = TRUE ; `the contract states the provider's duty to give information and report` = TRUE ; `the contract states the contingency, remedy and compensation if the provider cannot or does not perform` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to supervise, control and audit, and separate accounting` = TRUE ; `the contract restricts subcontracting` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to keep data and customer information confidential` = TRUE ; `the contract states the way of resolving disputes` = TRUE
@@fx `an oral outsourcing contract` : `An outsourcing` ; `the contract states scope and content` = TRUE ; `the contract states time and place` = TRUE ; `the contract states the rights and obligations of both sides` = TRUE ; `the contract states quality standards and requirements` = TRUE ; `the contract states the provider's duty to give information and report` = TRUE ; `the contract states the contingency, remedy and compensation if the provider cannot or does not perform` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to supervise, control and audit, and separate accounting` = TRUE ; `the contract restricts subcontracting` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to keep data and customer information confidential` = TRUE ; `the contract states the way of resolving disputes` = TRUE
@@fx `a written outsourcing contract that omits dispute resolution` : `An outsourcing` ; `the outsourcing contract is in writing` = TRUE ; `the contract states scope and content` = TRUE ; `the contract states time and place` = TRUE ; `the contract states the rights and obligations of both sides` = TRUE ; `the contract states quality standards and requirements` = TRUE ; `the contract states the provider's duty to give information and report` = TRUE ; `the contract states the contingency, remedy and compensation if the provider cannot or does not perform` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to supervise, control and audit, and separate accounting` = TRUE ; `the contract restricts subcontracting` = TRUE ; `the contract states the mechanism to keep data and customer information confidential` = TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` `outsourcing of claims handling`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` `outsourcing of internal audit`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` `outsourcing of internal control`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` `outsourcing of risk management`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` `outsourcing of selling`
#ASSERT `Dieu 90(2)(dd): the provider and any subcontracting meet the Law's requirements` `a provider that performs 75 percent itself`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(2)(dd): the provider and any subcontracting meet the Law's requirements` `a provider that performs 74 percent itself`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(2)(dd): the provider and any subcontracting meet the Law's requirements` `a provider that performs 80 percent and subcontracts without consent`
#ASSERT `Dieu 90(2)(dd): the provider and any subcontracting meet the Law's requirements` `a provider that performs 80 percent and subcontracts with consent`
#ASSERT `Dieu 90(3): the outsourcing contract is in the form and has the contents the Law requires` `a complete outsourcing contract`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(3): the outsourcing contract is in the form and has the contents the Law requires` `an oral outsourcing contract`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 90(3): the outsourcing contract is in the form and has the contents the Law requires` `a written outsourcing contract that omits dispute resolution`

§§ `Dieu 91, 92 and 93`

@@q 1931 1979
@ref Dieu 91-93 (src:1931-1979)
@@fx `a transfer the Ministry required` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the Ministry of Finance required it under Dieu 113(8)(c) or (d)` = TRUE
@@fx `a transfer on narrowing the scope` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `it narrows the content or scope of activity` = TRUE
@@fx `a transfer on a merger` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `it follows a division, split, merger, consolidation, dissolution or cessation` = TRUE
@@fx `a transfer on a revocation` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `it follows a revocation under Dieu 75(1)(a), (d) or (e)` = TRUE
@@fx `a transfer for a commercial reason` : `A portfolio transfer`
#ASSERT `Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` `a transfer the Ministry required`
#ASSERT `Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` `a transfer on narrowing the scope`
#ASSERT `Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` `a transfer on a merger`
#ASSERT `Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` `a transfer on a revocation`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` `a transfer for a commercial reason`
@@fx `a fit receiver` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the receiving insurer is already carrying on the line transferred` = TRUE ; `the receiving insurer meets the capital adequacy ratio and solvency requirements` = TRUE ; `the receiving insurer meets the conditions to run the line after receipt` = TRUE
@@fx `a receiver new to the line` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the receiving insurer meets the capital adequacy ratio and solvency requirements` = TRUE ; `the receiving insurer meets the conditions to run the line after receipt` = TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 92(1): the receiving insurer meets the conditions` `a fit receiver`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 92(1): the receiving insurer meets the conditions` `a receiver new to the line`
@@fx `assets equal to the reserve` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `value of the assets transferred` = 100 ; `technical reserve of the whole portfolio transferred` = 100
@@fx `assets short of the reserve in a required transfer` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the Ministry of Finance required it under Dieu 113(8)(c) or (d)` = TRUE ; `value of the assets transferred` = 90 ; `technical reserve of the whole portfolio transferred` = 100
@@fx `assets short of the reserve in a voluntary transfer` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `it narrows the content or scope of activity` = TRUE ; `value of the assets transferred` = 90 ; `technical reserve of the whole portfolio transferred` = 100
#ASSERT `Dieu 92(2): the assets transferred correspond to the technical reserve` `assets equal to the reserve`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 92(2): the assets transferred correspond to the technical reserve` `assets short of the reserve in a voluntary transfer`
#ASSERT `Dieu 92(3): the receiving insurer must agree a reduction of sums insured or benefits with the policyholders` `assets short of the reserve in a required transfer`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 92(3): the receiving insurer must agree a reduction of sums insured or benefits with the policyholders` `assets short of the reserve in a voluntary transfer`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 92(3): the receiving insurer must agree a reduction of sums insured or benefits with the policyholders` `assets equal to the reserve`
@@fx `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 31 March` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` = TRUE ; `date the Ministry of Finance approved` = YMD 2025 3 1 ; `date the transferor published and notified the policyholders` = YMD 2025 3 31
@@fx `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 1 April` : `A portfolio transfer` ; `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` = TRUE ; `date the Ministry of Finance approved` = YMD 2025 3 1 ; `date the transferor published and notified the policyholders` = YMD 2025 4 1
@@fx `a transfer not approved` : `A portfolio transfer`
#ASSERT `Dieu 93(1): the transfer may go ahead` `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 31 March`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 93(1): the transfer may go ahead` `a transfer not approved`
#ASSERT `Dieu 93(2): the last day to publish and notify the policyholders` `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 31 March` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 31
#ASSERT `Dieu 93(2): the publication and notice were in time` `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 31 March`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 93(2): the publication and notice were in time` `a transfer approved on 1 March, notified on 1 April`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 93(3): the Government's rules on the dossier, order and procedure of transferring a portfolio`
